<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pamunkey</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pamunkey are a Native American people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, the most powerful member of the Powhatan Confederacy, living along the Pamunkey River. Their leaders <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/opechancanough">Opechancanough</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cockacoeske">Cockacoeske</a> dealt with the English colony in the 17th century, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-middle-plantation">Treaty of Middle Plantation</a> of 1677 confirmed their reserved lands. Their reservation in King William County is among the oldest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>, and the tribe gained federal recognition in 2015.</p></div>
